WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.460
<b>Mr. Iceburg</b>

3
00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:56.320
[LUFFY]
This is great! Hahahahaha!

4
00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.580
You're the best, horse fish!

5
00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:01.490
[USOPP]
We might not be
traveling in style,

6
00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.720
but I gotta admit,
this sure is handy!

7
00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.230
I never thought riding
a fish would be so comfy!

8
00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:07.660
[CHILD A]
Over here! Over here!

9
00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.200
[CHILD B]
'Kay, here it comes!

10
00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:10.800
[CHILD C]
No problem!

11
00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.340
[CHILD D]
Oh no! It's too high!

12
00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:12.940
[CHILD A]
Get ready!

13
00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:13.570
[CHILD B]
Watch out!

14
00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:14.710
[CHILD A]
I got it!

15
00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.860
[CHILD C]
Ah man, no fair!
You did that last time, too!

16
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.670
[CHILD D]
I was gonna get that one!

17
00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.580
I wanna play, too!

18
00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:25.750
[USOPP]
Ahhh...

19
00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.920
I didn't think there'd be canals
running by people's houses, too!

20
00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:30.350
They're everywhere!

21
00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:33.420
[NAMI]
I'm trying to follow the map,

22
00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.460
but I don't want
to miss anything!

23
00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.430
Hey there, buddy!

24
00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.030
[LUFFY]
Right back at 'cha!

25
00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.960
[MAN D]
Hey!
You with the long nose!

26
00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:44.060
Huh?

27
00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:47.050
Uh, we're about to go against the flow.

28
00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:50.560
Is that okay? We're not
supposed to go up, are we?

29
00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.490
[NAMI]
Wait, wrong way!
Go right! Right!

30
00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:02.540
Awesome! You horse fish
can swim uphill, too?!

31
00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:04.540
What can't you do?!

32
00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:09.840
[LUFFY]
Look! The canals go
on top of the buildings!

33
00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:10.740
[NAMI]
Who cares?!

34
00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.950
We're going the wrong way!

35
00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:15.120
We need to go to the shopping district!

36
00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.870
Why? What's the rush?

37
00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:19.870
You wanna see the rest
of the city, don't you?

38
00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.910
[USOPP]
Ahhh! Look! Look!
Do something! Turn around!

39
00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:27.080
[LUFFY laughs]
Oh yeah,

40
00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:28.750
we're up pretty
high, aren't we?

41
00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:31.720
[USOPP]
That not what I want to hear.

42
00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.000
Aaaaaahhh! Help me!

43
00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.260
We're falling, we're
falling, we're falling,

44
00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:53.790
we're falling, we're falling,
we're falling, we're falling!

45
00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:09.780
[NAMI]
UGH!
Stop showing off!

46
00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:14.650
Huh?

47
00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:17.960
[MERCHANT MAN A]
Best prices
in town! Check us out!

48
00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:19.210
[MERCHANT MAN B]
Take a look over here!

49
00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:20.640
I promise you won't regret it!

50
00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.180
[MERCHANT MAN C]
We're
starting our 50% off sale!

51
00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:23.240
Don't miss it!

52
00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:28.980
[MERCHANT MAN D]
We've got rare goods

53
00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:31.420
for the distinguished customer!

54
00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.520
[LUFFY]
Ah! Oh man!
Check out all the stuff!

55
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.290
[NAMI]
We ended up in the
shopping district after all!

56
00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.480
Wait. You guys took
a shortcut, didn't you?

57
00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:43.280
I'm sorry!

58
00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.950
You're a lot smarter
than I gave you credit for!

59
00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:48.190
[USOPP]
This has gotta be the
biggest market I've ever seen!

60
00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.960
[LUFFY]
Uh-huh.
Whoa! Look!

61
00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.460
That bull is huge!

62
00:04:52.490 --> 00:04:55.560
[USOPP]
Whoa! Should we move?
It's coming straight at us!

63
00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:02.690
[USOPP]
That thing is scary!

64
00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.190
[LUFFY]
You think he eats people?

65
00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.320
[NAMI]
I wonder if this
one is a "King"?

66
00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.660
Huh? What's with them?

67
00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:12.430
They're all wearing
masks. That's weird.

68
00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:14.830
Wow. Neat. They're pretty.

69
00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.770
They must be going to a party.

70
00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:20.670
What's up? See something?

71
00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.610
Freshly made water-water
octopus dumplings for sale!

72
00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:28.180
Three water-water
croquettes, coming up!

73
00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.990
I didn't know they sold food!

74
00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:32.360
I'm hungry!
Let's buy everything!

75
00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:35.080
Wait! Go back!

76
00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:37.180
[USOPP]
Hey, Luffy!
Where're you going?!

77
00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:39.980
I dunno... Ask my ride!

78
00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.120
[NAMI and USOPP]
– Huh?
– Huh?

79
00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:48.930
Hello, there!
How may I help you?

80
00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.600
I see,so you
were hungry, too!

81
00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:52.540
[MERCHANT LADY B]
Water-water meat

82
00:05:52.570 --> 00:05:54.200
is the Yagara's favorite food.

83
00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:56.340
Although we usually cook it for humans.

84
00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:59.420
Meat, huh?
I'll take ten please!

85
00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:00.910
[MERCHANT LADY B]
They're so good that the cooks

86
00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:03.260
from the Gourmet Town
come buy them in secret!

87
00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:05.620
Bet you've never had
anything like it, huh?

88
00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:14.200
So soft! Yummy!

89
00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.670
Whoa, really? They're good?!

90
00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:17.300
Let me try one, Luffy!

91
00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:20.340
No way! I'm not sharing!

92
00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:22.180
[USOPP]
Nami, he's being mean!

93
00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:24.710
Make him share with me!

94
00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.010
[NAMI]
More masks.

95
00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.180
People all over town are wearing them.

96
00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.020
[USOPP]
Nami!

97
00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:31.520
[NAMI]
There's something
strange about this.

98
00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:35.130
[USOPP]
Nami! Are you listening?!

99
00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:38.450
[NAMI]
This is it.

100
00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:40.350
As soon as we take
the water gate elevator,

101
00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:43.120
we'll be at shipbuilding
island in no time.

102
00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:47.230
What's this water gate thing?

103
00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.360
[NAMI]
It's that tower
right ahead of us.

104
00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:58.130
[ELEVATOR GIRL A]
Attention everyone!

105
00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:01.120
The elevator is ready to go.

106
00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.990
Bulls and riders enter now!

107
00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.860
[ELEVATOR GIRL A]
Proceed in
an orderly fashion, please!

108
00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:07.860
All aboard for
shipbuilding island

109
00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:11.340
and downtown
Water Seven at this time!

110
00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:14.050
Passengers should enter the elevator quickly.

111
00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:17.180
The gate will be closing
in only one minute!

112
00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:22.220
Something crazy's gonna
happen, I just know it!

113
00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:30.220
[LUFFY]
The gate closed! It's starting!

114
00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:33.460
[USOPP]
We're going up!
We're going up! We're going up!

115
00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:40.130
I see! First you go in.
The gate shuts.

116
00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:41.600
The water fills the elevator,

117
00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:44.730
and then everybody
floats to the top!

118
00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:48.500
I still don't get it
but it sure is awesome!

119
00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:52.470
[NAMI]
They really do use
water for everything here!

120
00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:01.120
[SANJI]
Hey!

121
00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:04.400
[mumbling]
Who you callin' Moss Head, jerk?

122
00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:06.640
You awake?

123
00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:07.760
Huh...?

124
00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:09.220
You know where Robin went?

125
00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:11.190
She's not on the ship.

126
00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:12.530
Hmmm...

127
00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.580
Oh, I remember.

128
00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:17.410
She... uh... said she was
going out with Chopper.

129
00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:18.290
What?

130
00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:20.590
They were doing
some shopping, I think.

131
00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:21.720
[SANJI]
What the hell?!

132
00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:24.790
Does that mean I'm stuck
on this ship alone with you?!

133
00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:27.850
That's gotta be the most boring thing in the world!

134
00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:31.150
[ZORO]
Yep. That's why I'm sleeping.

135
00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:32.880
Fine. I need to do
our grocery shopping,

136
00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:34.720
so I'm taking off, too.

137
00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:36.640
Take good care of the boat while I'm gone.

138
00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.450
[snores]

139
00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:43.400
Asleep already, huh?
Whatever.

140
00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.200
Keep up the good work.

141
00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:16.700
[LUFFY]
We made it!

142
00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:21.550
[LUFFY]
So this is the best shipyard

143
00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:23.320
in the whole world, huh?

144
00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:26.120
It's even fancier than the rest of the town!

145
00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:32.860
[USOPP]
They've got a lot
more ground to work with

146
00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:35.800
than the residential
district, that's for sure.

147
00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.430
Everything's huge! So cool!

148
00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:46.650
Of course it's cool,
this place is the best!

149
00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:57.650
[USOPP]
There's a bunch
of people over there.

150
00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.650
Think something's going on at the shipyard?

151
00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:02.920
[LUFFY]
Let's go check
it out! Go, Yagara!

152
00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:11.090
[WOMAN B]
Look! Over there!

153
00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:14.700
It's Lucci!
He's so handsome!

154
00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:16.380
[BUSYBODY MAN A]
Paulie's here today too, right?

155
00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:18.260
[BUSYBODY MAN B]
Who cares
about those guys, huh?!

156
00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:20.120
Now Lulu, that's a real man.

157
00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:22.260
Just look at that moustache!

158
00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:22.990
[BUSYBODY MAN C]
Whatever!

159
00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:25.990
Nobody's manlier than Tilestone!

160
00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:27.890
[LUFFY]
Hey mister.

161
00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:28.800
Hmm?

162
00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:30.270
What's this crowd about?

163
00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:32.740
Oh. It was just some
boneheaded pirates

164
00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:35.430
trying to pick a fight
with the shipwrights again.

165
00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:37.830
Y'know happens all the time.

166
00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:40.170
But our guys sent
'em packing, like always.

167
00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.710
Those pirates'll
never learn their lesson.

168
00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.010
Whoa, that's nuts.

169
00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:45.870
The shipwrights can beat up pirates?

170
00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:48.010
Ah, you must be tourists, huh?

171
00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.310
The shipwrights are, well...

172
00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:51.950
...they're like
celebrities to us.

173
00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:54.850
In fact, you might say that this crowd is their fan club.

174
00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:57.820
We're always watching
the Galley-La Company.

175
00:10:57.850 --> 00:10:59.160
They're strong.

176
00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:00.970
They're skilled.

177
00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.930
And they're the pride of
every citizen in Water Seven.

178
00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:10.850
Wow. I can't wait to meet them!

179
00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:13.560
[NAMI]
Hey, Luffy.

180
00:11:13.590 --> 00:11:14.630
[LUFFY]
Huh?

181
00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:17.600
Let's hurry up and get the gold traded in, okay?

182
00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:18.300
This is fun.

183
00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:19.930
But it can wait 'til later.

184
00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:33.170
<b>Backstreets Shopping District
Water Seven</b>

185
00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:34.710
[ROBIN]
It says that we're

186
00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:35.860
in the backstreet
shopping district.

187
00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:38.030
[CHOPPER]
It seems awfully
crowded for a backstreet,

188
00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:39.860
if you ask me.

189
00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:43.570
Kinda neat that they have places to walk around, though.

190
00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:46.000
They must've put a lot of
thought into the town's design.

191
00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:47.400
[CHOPPER]
Yeah.

192
00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:51.660
[CHOPPER]
What is that guy selling?!

193
00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:53.090
It looks creepy!

194
00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:55.330
[ROBIN]
It's just a mask shop.

195
00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:59.030
I noticed a lot of people
around town wearing them,

196
00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:00.330
so they must buy
them from there.

197
00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:01.400
It's something you wear?

198
00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:02.650
I thought that was their face!

199
00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:04.690
Wow that's a big relief!

200
00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:08.690
[ROBIN]
It seems the people here

201
00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:11.160
take the Sea Train
to San Faldo Island,

202
00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:13.460
where they hold a
costume carnival every day.

203
00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:14.920
[CHOPPER]
Huh? How do you know that?

204
00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:16.420
We just got here!

205
00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:18.960
[ROBIN]
The people walking
by are talking about it.

206
00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:22.390
[CHOPPER]
Whoa and you
hear everything they say?

207
00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:24.060
I can't help it.

208
00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:26.330
Ever since I was young,

209
00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:28.300
I've made it a habit
to keep a critical eye

210
00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:30.440
and ear on my environment.

211
00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:35.040
Wow, Robin that's cool.

212
00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:41.610
[ROBIN]
Huh... Doctor.

213
00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:42.680
[CHOPPER]
Hm?

214
00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:45.350
[ROBIN]
See that? I think
we found your bookstore.

215
00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.120
Oh! Really?

216
00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:50.290
Can we go inside now?!

217
00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:52.260
[ROBIN chuckles]
Of course. Be my guest.

218
00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.620
Today is the best day ever!

219
00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:09.270
[BLUENO]
CP9.

220
00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:27.660
Hey! What're you waiting for?!

221
00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:59.570
[thinking]
If I'm in my human
form maybe it'll be okay?

222
00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:03.480
My! What a funny mask!

223
00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:04.830
What's your costume?

224
00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:08.610
Oh... uh... a human reindeer?

225
00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:13.310
Hmm! Ahahaha! As long
as you're having fun, right?

226
00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:17.240
Hey, wait.

227
00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:24.380
Robin?

228
00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:28.320
[CHOPPER]
Hello? Robin?!

229
00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:09.060
Pity, I was hoping that we could kill you in your sleep.

230
00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:15.370
You bastards sure
got a lot of nerve.

231
00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:16.600
Who are you?

232
00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:20.080
[LUFFY]
O-One hundred million berries?!

233
00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:23.900
<b>Currency Exchange</b>

234
00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:21.350
[USOPP]
Keep it down, stupid!

235
00:15:21.380 --> 00:15:22.720
You want the whole
city to know how much

236
00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:24.190
cash we're lugging around?!

237
00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:26.690
[LUFFY]
You're really gonna give
us that much money, mister?!

238
00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:27.790
[USOPP]
Play it cool, Luffy!

239
00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:30.590
You gotta handle these things like a professional!

240
00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:31.530
[OWNER MAN A]
It may sound like a lot,

241
00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:33.130
but that's most
certainly what it's worth.

242
00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:36.970
It has historical value and high purity.

243
00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.500
With a hundred
million we can make

244
00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.170
the Merry even
better than before!

245
00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.510
[USOPP]
No kidding! And we'll
have plenty to spare!

246
00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:45.410
Then we'll spend the rest of on
a big statue to put on the deck!

247
00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:46.580
[LUFFY]
No. No, we won't.

248
00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:47.680
[OWNER MAN A]
Well that's wonderful,

249
00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:48.980
I'm glad you accept the amount.

250
00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:51.510
Now I need you thumbprint
and signature here.

251
00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:54.680
After that, I'll prepare your money lickety-split.

252
00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:56.670
[LUFFY]
You can have both
my thumbs if you want 'em!

253
00:15:56.670 --> 00:15:57.440
[USOPP]
Mine, too!

254
00:15:57.470 --> 00:15:59.900
The more thumbs
the better, right?

255
00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:12.150
What's up?
Giving him a toe print?

256
00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:13.290
Before we sign anything,

257
00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:18.700
there are three things I'd
like to say. Mr. Appraiser.

258
00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:21.400
First, I forgot
to mention this

259
00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:24.370
but he's got a one hundred
million bounty on his head.

260
00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:30.200
Second, I don't accept the appraisal you gave us.

261
00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:33.770
Third, if you try
to lie to us again.

262
00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:37.700
It'll be the last lie you
ever tell. You got that?

263
00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:41.390
[OWNER MAN A]
Please forgive me!

264
00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:44.490
Three hundred million?!

265
00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.690
This is like a dream come true!

266
00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:48.520
Skypeia paid off after all!

267
00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:50.360
I never thought I'd see the day!

268
00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:52.480
Y'know, I always
wanted to be filthy rich!

269
00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:54.040
It's our money, too!

270
00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:55.460
[OWNER MAN A]
Uh... p-pleasure
doing business with you.

271
00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:56.630
[USOPP]
I don't feel comfortable having

272
00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:58.600
all this money in
one place, guys!

273
00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:00.970
It's scary!
I mean, what if I trip

274
00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:03.440
and it all falls
out or something?

275
00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:07.650
That was great! You sure
were scary back there, Nami!

276
00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:09.780
I estimated 300
million from the start,

277
00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:11.880
but I figured he
wouldn't give it up easy.

278
00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:13.760
You really gotta work on your game face.

279
00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:14.680
Good thing I was there.

280
00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:15.650
Cut it out!

281
00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:18.620
You're making me nervous swinging that around!

282
00:17:18.650 --> 00:17:22.460
Well, whatever, we got our money
now and that's what matters.

283
00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:24.870
Aaaahhh!

284
00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:26.610
You dropped it!

285
00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:28.610
Don't let it fall in the river!

286
00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:35.480
Phew! That woulda been bad
if the money got wet, huh?

287
00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:40.390
If you lose my money,
you're paying in blood!

288
00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:43.560
I'm sorry. V-Very sorry.

289
00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:47.060
So please don't
break my face anymore.

290
00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:50.460
[FRANKY FAMILY NONECK]
Whoa, did you hear that?

291
00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:51.360
Sure did!

292
00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:03.000
You don't know
who we are?! Really?

293
00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:05.870
'Cause we sure know
you, Pirate Hunter!

294
00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:10.210
[ZAMBAI]
Babies stop crying
when they hear our name!

295
00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:13.540
A collection of bounty hunters.

296
00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:14.110
We are The Franky Family!

297
00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:14.810
Ain't no doubt about it,
those are the Straw Hats.

298
00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:16.580
was a sweet deal,
but this is way sweeter.

299
00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:17.540
Now, if you don't mind,

300
00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:19.580
I think we'll be taking
that 60 million bounty

301
00:18:19.610 --> 00:18:21.050
you've got on your head.

302
00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:21.950
When we're done with you,

303
00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:23.950
we'll wait inside
that cabin of yours

304
00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:25.330
and ambush the rest of your
crew when they get back!

305
00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:26.160
If we meet up with the rest

306
00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:27.400
of the gang and
get 'em to help us out,

307
00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:27.830
we can make twice the money
with only half the hard work!

308
00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:30.470
We're gonna be rolling in the dough in no time!

309
00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:33.970
It's my lucky day!

310
00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:38.080
Lucky, huh?

311
00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:43.980
We'll see about that,
now won't we?

312
00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:55.930
Two-Sword Style.

313
00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:57.100
Rhino...

314
00:18:57.130 --> 00:18:58.760
...Cycle!

315
00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:05.200
[sighs]

316
00:19:09.610 --> 00:19:11.080
Back to sleep.

317
00:19:13.280 --> 00:19:15.280
Ah... man!

318
00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:19.370
[USOPP]
I dunno, Nami.

319
00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:22.110
Maybe we should take the cash back to the ship after all.

320
00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:23.980
[NAMI]
That'd be a
complete waste of time.

321
00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:26.010
The shipyard is right around the corner.

322
00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:28.640
Come on. You don't
have to ride so far away.

323
00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:29.870
Let me play with the money.

324
00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:32.980
Anyway, we'll probably head
back to the Merry soon enough.

325
00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:34.270
After we meet
with the shipwrights,

326
00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:36.010
I'm sure they'll need
to look at the damages

327
00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:37.780
before they can
give us a quote.

328
00:19:37.810 --> 00:19:39.040
I didn't think of it that way.

329
00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:41.150
I guess I can watch
the money 'til then.

330
00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:43.580
I've never carried so much cash at once, that's all.

331
00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:44.920
I don't know how to handle it.

332
00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.650
[NAMI]
Well, that's only natural.

333
00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:47.790
Just don't flail it around

334
00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:49.960
and throw it in any
rivers and you'll be fine.

335
00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:52.140
[LUFFY]
Ooh! They're selling
water buns over there!

336
00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:53.260
Let's buy a hundred of 'em!

337
00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:54.260
[NAMI and USOPP]
– Shut up.
– Shut up.

338
00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:54.870
[LUFFY]
How 'bout a thousand?

339
00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:55.460
[NAMI and USOPP]
– Shut up.
– Shut up.

340
00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.060
[LUFFY]
How 'bout...

341
00:19:56.060 --> 00:19:56.560
[NAMI and USOPP]
– Shut up.
– Shut up.

342
00:19:57.120 --> 00:19:58.690
[LUFFY]
Okay.

343
00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:13.860
Right. Back to the shipyard.

344
00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:16.820
And it looks like the
crowd's cleared out, too.

345
00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:19.190
[USOPP chuckles]
Well, that's good.

346
00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:20.390
We have enough to deal

347
00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:22.800
with without the shipwright
fan club getting in the way.

348
00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.700
[LUFFY]
All we gotta do
is find that ice guy.

349
00:20:24.730 --> 00:20:27.970
Uh wait. What's
his name again?

350
00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:29.440
[NAMI]
It's Iceburg.

351
00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:31.570
Oh yeah, now
I remember... Ice Pops.

352
00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:32.970
The old lady back at
the train station said

353
00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:34.610
that's who we
needed to talk to,

354
00:20:34.640 --> 00:20:35.770
but now that
I think about it,

355
00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:37.600
we don't know anything
about him, do we?

356
00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:38.900
Well, it's the only lead we've got.

357
00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:40.680
I don't know even
how this place works.

358
00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:42.870
Is it okay to
just walk right in?

359
00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:44.540
[LUFFY]
That's what I'm doing!

360
00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:46.240
[NAMI and USOPP]
– Not again.
– Not again.

361
00:20:47.380 --> 00:20:49.510
Hold it right there.

362
00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:50.580
[KAKU]
You've got
a lot of gumption

363
00:20:50.610 --> 00:20:52.640
just waltzing in like that.

364
00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:54.310
[KAKU]
Why don't we
take a step over here.

365
00:20:54.340 --> 00:20:56.880
Then we can talk.

366
00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:58.580
Don't worry. It's not personal.

367
00:20:58.610 --> 00:20:59.950
You're outsiders is all.

368
00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:02.280
So you're not allowed inside the plant.

369
00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:06.620
[KAKU]
Upsey daisy.

370
00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:11.830
<b>Kaku
Shipwright
Galley-La Company</b>

371
00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:11.920
All right champ, what brings
you to the docks today?

372
00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:13.820
C'mon Usopp, I know it's you.

373
00:21:13.860 --> 00:21:16.730
I'm right here, Luffy. Idiot!

374
00:21:16.760 --> 00:21:19.000
Oh, now that I look at it, his nose is square.

375
00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:21.130
Anyway that aside.

376
00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:23.170
We came here to see
Iceburg, if that's all right.

377
00:21:23.200 --> 00:21:27.070
Hmm... Is that so, little
miss? Are you customers?

378
00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:28.470
Oh, that's nifty.

379
00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:30.010
Not every day that
youngsters come here

380
00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:32.680
with a letter of introduction
from Granny Kokoro.

381
00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:35.040
Uh... Hold on,
how old are you?

382
00:21:35.070 --> 00:21:36.800
I'm 23, why do you ask?

383
00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:38.950
You know, for someone who's
hardly any older than us,

384
00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:40.750
you sure do talk
like an old man.

385
00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:43.450
Hahahaha!
I get that a lot.

386
00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:44.880
So, do you know Iceburg,

387
00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:46.420
or did we come
to the wrong place?

388
00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:47.920
Well, of course I know Iceburg.

389
00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:49.790
Why, I'd say that
everyone here knows him,

390
00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:52.120
seeing as he's the
mayor of the city and all.

391
00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:56.400
Wow. Ice Pops is an
important guy, huh?

392
00:21:56.440 --> 00:21:57.810
[KAKU]
Darn skippy he is.

393
00:21:57.840 --> 00:22:00.040
He's also the president
of our Galley-La Company

394
00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:02.460
and manager of the
sea train on top of that.

395
00:22:02.490 --> 00:22:04.060
I didn't know he
was such a big deal!

396
00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:06.530
[KAKU]
I had a feeling you
weren't from around here.

397
00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:08.430
Iceburg is pretty
famous in these parts.

398
00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:09.930
But do you know where we can find him?

399
00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:12.970
[KAKU]
Hmmm, that's
the question, isn't it?

400
00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:14.770
He keeps pretty busy, of course.

401
00:22:14.800 --> 00:22:17.400
Hunting him down can be a chore sometimes.

402
00:22:17.420 --> 00:22:18.920
[NAMI]
But you work for him, right?

403
00:22:18.960 --> 00:22:20.620
Can't you get in touch somehow?

404
00:22:20.640 --> 00:22:21.710
I suppose I could,

405
00:22:21.740 --> 00:22:23.750
but it seems like you're
in a hurry to get this done.

406
00:22:23.780 --> 00:22:25.010
[NAMI]
Not exactly, but...

407
00:22:26.340 --> 00:22:29.020
Hahahaha...
It's fine, I understand.

408
00:22:29.020 --> 00:22:31.490
You're itching to have your ship looked at, right?

409
00:22:32.100 --> 00:22:33.870
Where did you anchor it?

410
00:22:33.900 --> 00:22:35.900
Uh, it's over
by the rocky cape.

411
00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:38.680
[KAKU]
All-righty then. I'll
skedaddle over there real quick.

412
00:22:38.720 --> 00:22:40.720
If I take a gander at
your ship beforehand,

413
00:22:40.810 --> 00:22:43.210
you can start talking cost
with Iceburg right away.

414
00:22:43.240 --> 00:22:45.050
As I said, he's very busy,

415
00:22:45.080 --> 00:22:47.050
so I'm sure he'll
be grateful as well.

416
00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:50.650
Wait, skedaddle like how?
On a Yagara or what?

417
00:22:50.690 --> 00:22:51.790
[KAKU]
Hahahaha.

418
00:22:51.820 --> 00:22:54.590
I thought we were
trying to save time!

419
00:22:54.620 --> 00:22:56.190
If you folks can hang
tight for ten minutes,

420
00:22:56.220 --> 00:22:58.760
I should be back in two
shakes of a lamb's tail.

421
00:22:58.760 --> 00:23:00.860
Just ten minutes?

422
00:23:00.900 --> 00:23:03.630
[KAKU]
That's right.
Or your money back.

423
00:23:06.510 --> 00:23:07.820
[LUFFY]
Whoa!

424
00:23:09.970 --> 00:23:12.980
[USOPP]
He's fast!

425
00:23:13.010 --> 00:23:14.980
[KAKU]
Alley-oop!

426
00:23:14.980 --> 00:23:18.050
WHOA! He flew!

427
00:23:20.090 --> 00:23:21.790
Wait, where's he going?

428
00:23:21.830 --> 00:23:23.530
If he jumps off
the edge he'll...

429
00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:24.860
[ALL THREE]
– Fall!
– Fall!

430
00:23:24.890 --> 00:23:27.490
No! Come back!

431
00:23:32.090 --> 00:23:34.660
Hahaha!

432
00:23:35.860 --> 00:23:37.630
So cool!

433
00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:39.960
Yeah, but is he gonna be okay?

434
00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:41.160
Don't worry.

435
00:23:41.190 --> 00:23:43.400
He's always soaring through town.

436
00:23:44.280 --> 00:23:44.980
Huh?

437
00:23:45.410 --> 00:23:48.410
[ICEBURG]
They call
him the "Mountain Wind."

438
00:23:48.450 --> 00:23:49.590
If you didn't know,

439
00:23:49.650 --> 00:23:53.490
he's the Galley-La Company's
Dock One Carpentry Foreman.

440
00:23:54.870 --> 00:23:55.830
Kaku.

441
00:24:00.070 --> 00:24:03.970
[SANJI]
I see. So this
is the city of water, huh?

442
00:24:04.030 --> 00:24:05.460
Pretty impressive place.

443
00:24:05.550 --> 00:24:07.660
Lives up to its name, that's for sure.

444
00:24:07.690 --> 00:24:08.860
I mean, look around!

445
00:24:08.890 --> 00:24:11.030
Clean water,
clean streets, fresh food,

446
00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:13.660
and most importantly,
plenty of cute girls.

447
00:24:13.700 --> 00:24:15.240
This place has it all.

448
00:24:15.270 --> 00:24:16.540
Take my word for it,

449
00:24:16.570 --> 00:24:17.740
this is the
perfect place to take

450
00:24:17.770 --> 00:24:20.840
that special someone
on a romantic stroll.

451
00:24:20.880 --> 00:24:24.550
But why stop at one when I have two lovely ladies?

452
00:24:26.290 --> 00:24:29.600
This one is Nami and
this one here is Robin!

453
00:24:30.020 --> 00:24:32.160
[SHOP LADY A]
You're
scaring away the customers!

454
00:24:32.190 --> 00:24:33.360
Stop making that creepy face

455
00:24:33.390 --> 00:24:36.100
and tell me which water-water
cabbage you want already!

456
00:24:36.130 --> 00:24:37.160
I'll take both of them.

457
00:24:37.200 --> 00:24:39.200
Oh, and there was something I wanted to ask you.

458
00:24:39.230 --> 00:24:40.740
I'm looking for
some local specialties

459
00:24:40.770 --> 00:24:42.270
that're in season right now.

460
00:24:42.300 --> 00:24:43.470
So what've you got?

461
00:24:43.830 --> 00:24:47.090
[SANJI]
Let's see uh this way?

462
00:24:47.540 --> 00:24:50.400
This place sure is a pain when you have to walk.

463
00:24:52.870 --> 00:24:54.280
If I don't stop
running into dead ends

464
00:24:54.310 --> 00:24:56.280
and start figuring out
where the hell I am.

465
00:24:56.310 --> 00:24:59.180
This food's gonna go bad before
I make it back to the Merry.

466
00:24:59.210 --> 00:25:01.020
Don't tell me
Zoro's brain fungus

467
00:25:01.040 --> 00:25:03.310
is starting to
spread to me, too.

468
00:25:09.480 --> 00:25:12.920
Oh! Robin, boy am
I glad to see you!

469
00:25:12.950 --> 00:25:15.950
It's me, Sanji! Yoo hoo!

470
00:25:15.990 --> 00:25:18.360
Robin! Look!

471
00:25:19.420 --> 00:25:20.920
Huh?

472
00:25:21.810 --> 00:25:23.500
She disappeared.

473
00:25:24.020 --> 00:25:26.290
Looks like another
dead-end to me.

474
00:25:27.020 --> 00:25:29.860
The only way to go
is up, but there's...

475
00:25:33.080 --> 00:25:34.380
Usopp?

476
00:25:34.980 --> 00:25:37.720
Man, I don't know what's up with this place.

477
00:25:38.320 --> 00:25:40.420
I'm not going crazy, am I?

478
00:25:52.690 --> 00:25:56.230
[KAKU]
Well lookie here.
That must be the one.

479
00:25:59.710 --> 00:26:00.910
[KAKU]
Pardon me.

480
00:26:04.260 --> 00:26:06.760
[thinking]
Oh, it's just Usopp.

481
00:26:07.030 --> 00:26:08.030
My goodness,

482
00:26:08.060 --> 00:26:09.660
I know they told me
their ship needed repairs,

483
00:26:09.700 --> 00:26:12.070
but I didn't think it
would be in shambles!

484
00:26:15.040 --> 00:26:18.140
We should start by replacing this mast.

485
00:26:19.970 --> 00:26:22.710
[ZORO thinking]
Wait. That's not right.

486
00:26:22.800 --> 00:26:25.470
Hey, I see you!
Don't move! You hear me?!

487
00:26:25.500 --> 00:26:28.810
Oh pardon. I didn't
intend to disturb your nap.

488
00:26:28.840 --> 00:26:31.180
[USOPP]
Jeez! That was
a big surprise!

489
00:26:31.210 --> 00:26:34.210
[LUFFY]
I've never seen
someone jump that far before!

490
00:26:34.240 --> 00:26:35.910
[ICEBURG]
Mmwell, my craftsmen are

491
00:26:35.950 --> 00:26:38.090
the best in the
business for a reason.

492
00:26:38.090 --> 00:26:39.060
Who is this guy?

493
00:26:39.100 --> 00:26:40.000
Don't ask me.

494
00:26:40.030 --> 00:26:42.000
[ICEBURG]
Extraordinary
ships are not born

495
00:26:42.030 --> 00:26:43.400
from ordinary circumstances.

496
00:26:43.430 --> 00:26:47.000
They require a nearly superhuman level of skill.

497
00:26:47.040 --> 00:26:48.000
By the way, Kalifa.

498
00:26:48.040 --> 00:26:49.950
I've already finished the background check.

499
00:26:49.950 --> 00:26:52.050
The one in the middle is Straw Hat Luffy.

500
00:26:52.080 --> 00:26:56.620
His crew also includes Pirate Hunter Zoro and Nico Robin.

501
00:26:56.620 --> 00:26:59.160
Their combined bounty is two
hundred thirty-nine million.

502
00:26:59.190 --> 00:27:01.520
They have four other members
without posted bounties.

503
00:27:01.990 --> 00:27:03.430
And their crew was
formed in the East Blue.

504
00:27:04.350 --> 00:27:05.350
Named after their captain,

505
00:27:05.390 --> 00:27:08.020
they're known simply
as the Straw Hat Pirates.

506
00:27:08.060 --> 00:27:09.460
[thinking]
They've really
got our number.

507
00:27:09.480 --> 00:27:14.400
<b>Iceburg
Water Seven Mayor
&
Galley-La Company President</b>

508
00:27:09.540 --> 00:27:12.980
I see. Welcome.
My name is Iceburg.

509
00:27:13.010 --> 00:27:14.650
I'm the boss here.

510
00:27:14.680 --> 00:27:17.090
And this is a mouse I just picked up.

511
00:27:17.120 --> 00:27:21.590
Its name is... let's see... Tyrannosaurus.

512
00:27:21.700 --> 00:27:23.670
I'll need some rodent food and a cage.

513
00:27:23.700 --> 00:27:25.740
[KALIFA]
I've already
taken care of that, Sir.

514
00:27:25.770 --> 00:27:27.640
Mmwell! Amazing work, Kalifa!

515
00:27:27.670 --> 00:27:30.610
Just doing my job.
Speaking of which.

516
00:27:30.640 --> 00:27:32.680
You're due at a hotel
in Chiza for lunch

517
00:27:32.720 --> 00:27:34.520
with a glassware
factory executive.

518
00:27:34.560 --> 00:27:36.260
After that, you're
set to make a speech

519
00:27:36.290 --> 00:27:38.490
at Liguria Square and
once that's finished.

520
00:27:38.530 --> 00:27:41.570
You'll be meeting with
Mr. Bimine, the mayor of Pucci.

521
00:27:41.600 --> 00:27:42.430
Their local newspaper

522
00:27:42.470 --> 00:27:44.770
is scheduled to
interview you as well.

523
00:27:44.770 --> 00:27:46.410
Oh, and when you
return to the office,

524
00:27:46.440 --> 00:27:48.180
there's a folder full
of important documents

525
00:27:48.200 --> 00:27:50.340
I need your signature on.

526
00:27:50.370 --> 00:27:52.070
I don't wanna.

527
00:27:52.440 --> 00:27:54.730
Very well, then I'll cancel
everything for you.

528
00:27:55.250 --> 00:27:57.320
Hold on, you're
not serious are you?!

529
00:27:57.340 --> 00:27:58.380
[ICEBURG]
What's the point in having power

530
00:27:58.410 --> 00:28:00.450
if I don't get
to do what I want?

531
00:28:00.480 --> 00:28:01.480
If that's how you run things,

532
00:28:01.520 --> 00:28:03.460
you've gotta be the
worst mayor in the world!

533
00:28:03.480 --> 00:28:05.270
Yeah Pops, that's pretty lazy.

534
00:28:05.270 --> 00:28:07.140
So hold on, are you
sure this is the guy

535
00:28:07.220 --> 00:28:08.620
that old lady
was talking about?

536
00:28:08.620 --> 00:28:10.990
Uh-huh. He's the
guy, all right.

537
00:28:11.020 --> 00:28:13.090
[KALIFA]
How dare you!

538
00:28:19.400 --> 00:28:21.070
What's the big idea, lady?!

539
00:28:21.100 --> 00:28:22.530
[NAMI]
That was scary!

540
00:28:28.350 --> 00:28:33.480
<b>Kalifa
Iceburg's Beautiful Secretary</b>

541
00:28:28.570 --> 00:28:30.640
I won't stand here and
let you insolent louts

542
00:28:30.680 --> 00:28:33.580
disrespect one of the
world's leading ship engineers.

543
00:28:33.580 --> 00:28:34.710
Hey, what's going on over there?

544
00:28:34.750 --> 00:28:36.350
Iceburg's
secretary just flipped out

545
00:28:36.420 --> 00:28:37.650
on some pirates, again!

546
00:28:37.650 --> 00:28:39.420
I wish she'd flip out on me!

547
00:28:39.550 --> 00:28:40.480
Pardon me.

548
00:28:40.520 --> 00:28:42.490
I get a bit carried away from time to time.

549
00:28:42.520 --> 00:28:45.290
Still, Iceburg is a respected
figure here in Water Seven,

550
00:28:45.320 --> 00:28:47.360
so try to show some courtesy.

551
00:28:47.390 --> 00:28:49.630
Yes. Please don't
provoke Kalifa.

552
00:28:49.720 --> 00:28:51.820
When she lashes out in anger...

553
00:28:52.290 --> 00:28:54.330
...her aim sucks.

554
00:28:54.970 --> 00:28:57.340
We might've hurt his feelings,
but you hurt his face!

555
00:28:57.370 --> 00:28:58.840
You're way meaner than us!

556
00:28:58.870 --> 00:29:01.280
Putting all that behind us,
if you're Iceburg,

557
00:29:01.310 --> 00:29:02.510
you're the man
we're looking for.

558
00:29:02.540 --> 00:29:05.640
Here, we brought a letter of introduction for you to look at.

559
00:29:05.340 --> 00:29:09.930
<b>Take a look at their ship.</b>
<b>Kokoro</b>

560
00:29:05.670 --> 00:29:08.280
From Granny Kokoro?

561
00:29:08.310 --> 00:29:10.840
Take a look at
their ship it says.

562
00:29:09.930 --> 00:29:10.310
<b>Take a look at their ship.</b>
<b>Kokoro</b>

563
00:29:11.110 --> 00:29:12.550
Aaaah!

564
00:29:12.580 --> 00:29:14.220
What?! Are you serious?!

565
00:29:14.250 --> 00:29:16.480
There has to be something
we can do to change your mind!

566
00:29:16.520 --> 00:29:18.330
If money's the
issue, we can pay!

567
00:29:18.330 --> 00:29:19.330
If you're really the best,

568
00:29:19.570 --> 00:29:21.540
then you've gotta be
the one to fix our Merry!

569
00:29:21.570 --> 00:29:22.770
C'mon, we're begging!

570
00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:23.770
[ICEBURG]
Okay.

571
00:29:23.800 --> 00:29:25.570
That's it?! You don't
need to think about it?

572
00:29:25.610 --> 00:29:26.410
[ICEBURG]
Nope.

573
00:29:26.440 --> 00:29:27.740
Then why'd you
tear up the letter?!

574
00:29:27.750 --> 00:29:29.520
The lipstick mark
was creeping me out.

575
00:29:29.560 --> 00:29:30.860
Even so, Granny Kokoro and I

576
00:29:30.870 --> 00:29:32.600
have been drinking
buddies for years.

577
00:29:32.660 --> 00:29:34.730
Mmwell and since
Kaku has already gone

578
00:29:34.760 --> 00:29:35.790
to make an assessment for me,

579
00:29:35.830 --> 00:29:37.630
it would seem like a
waste to turn you down now.

580
00:29:37.690 --> 00:29:40.590
Wouldn't you say?

581
00:29:40.620 --> 00:29:42.790
Besides, it's not like I had anything better to do.

582
00:29:42.800 --> 00:29:44.670
Let me show you around
the factory, sound good?

583
00:29:44.700 --> 00:29:46.440
[LUFFY]
Sweet! Bring it on!

584
00:29:46.470 --> 00:29:47.470
Come along with me then.

585
00:29:47.470 --> 00:29:48.640
Did he seriously
cancel all of his

586
00:29:48.680 --> 00:29:50.510
meetings just
to give us a tour?

587
00:29:50.540 --> 00:29:54.180
Yeah! You gotta let me sit
on all the cool ships, okay?

588
00:29:54.210 --> 00:29:56.450
[USOPP]
Oh, right... the money.

589
00:29:56.480 --> 00:30:00.720
Wait, what? No!
No, no, no, no, no!

590
00:30:00.750 --> 00:30:03.760
NOOOOO!

591
00:30:03.790 --> 00:30:07.030
Hey! What's wrong
Usopp? Come on!

592
00:30:07.600 --> 00:30:10.400
The-The-The money...
It... it disappeared!

593
00:30:10.400 --> 00:30:11.540
[NAMI]
Did you drop it somewhere?!

594
00:30:13.430 --> 00:30:15.600
[USOPP]
I don't know!

595
00:30:19.300 --> 00:30:27.820
Hey! Over there!

596
00:30:27.820 --> 00:30:29.690
[USOPP]
Wait! Who are you?!

597
00:30:29.720 --> 00:30:32.830
Why are you taking our money...
I mean, give it back!

598
00:30:32.860 --> 00:30:36.830
We need it, you jerks!
Do you hear me?! Hey!

599
00:30:36.860 --> 00:30:38.570
[chuckles]

600
00:30:38.600 --> 00:30:40.370
Thanks for the cash!

601
00:30:40.510 --> 00:30:45.190
[USOPP]
Give us our money back!
